# ---------------- Resources.events (RTS resource names) ----------------
# Which resources the economy knows about. Every resource is just a global variable; this file
# only tells the engine the names, so `Minerals is higher than 50`, `enough Minerals for Barracks`,
# `<Building><Resource>Cost`, `when resources change` and `add 5 to Credits` all work on them.
#
# HOW IT LOADS: the file is read by name — Resources.events — once at load and again on hot
# reload, BEFORE the other sheets are parsed, so a name or spelling declared here is understood by
# every sheet in the game. Attaching it to a sheet is optional; the `when game starts` block below
# keeps it valid as a normal event file.
#
# TO ADD YOUR OWN RESOURCE: add its name to the `Resources` list (and its cost variables in your
# building sheets, e.g. `set BarracksCreditsCost to 150`). No code change is needed. To rename a
# whole economy, replace the list — StarCraft's Minerals/Gas, Red Alert's Ore/Gems/Power and
# Homeworld's RUs are all in the default list already.
#
# NO FILE, NO PROBLEM: with this file missing (or declaring nothing) the built-in nine below are
# used, so scenes authored before it existed behave exactly as before.

when game starts
  # ---- the resources, in the order `when resources change` reports them ------------------
  set Resources to "Minerals, Gas, SupplyUsed, SupplyMax, FoodCap, Ore, Gems, Power, RUs"

  # ---- extra spellings: `Canonical=alias,alias; Canonical2=alias` -------------------------
  # The built-in ones (`mineral`, `supply used`, `food`, `ru`, …) keep working; these are on top.
  set ResourceAliases to "Minerals=minerals,min; SupplyUsed=supply used,supplied; SupplyMax=supply max,max supply; FoodCap=food cap; Gems=gem; RUs=ru,resource units"

  # ---- what supply means in this game -----------------------------------------------------
  # `SupplyUsedResource` is the "used" counter, `SupplyCapResource` the ceiling, and the fallback
  # is read when the ceiling was never set (Red Alert's food cap).
  set SupplyUsedResource to "SupplyUsed"
  set SupplyCapResource to "SupplyMax"
  set SupplyCapFallbackResource to "FoodCap"

  # ---- which resource `<Building>Cost` means ----------------------------------------------
  # `set BarracksCost to 150` charges this resource; `<Building>GasCost` etc. name others.
  set DefaultCostResource to "Minerals"
